# A claim written before a retirement raises the entry after it: the raise
# checks only the entry, which the retirement reset, so an epoch the old
# incarnation already superseded is raised and its activation appends.
MODULE: StaleEpochNeverAppendsRaiseIgnoresRetiredFloor
TARGET: StaleEpochNeverAppends
CLASS: Invariant
EXPECT: clean (a redundancy check: the guard is implied in the model and kept for the reason in LiveAdvanceDesign.md)
SUMMARY: the claim's raise is not refused at or below the retired floor
PERTURBS: ClaimRaise
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] >= Max2(fence, memFence)
    /\ epoch[a] > retired
--- REPLACE
    /\ epoch[a] >= Max2(fence, memFence)
\* MUTATION: the retired floor is not checked at the raise.
--- END